Every clinician should ensure a mild-to-moderate-full-agonist-opioid-withdrawal for a patient before a first-buprenorphine-dose.
If a patient takes a full-agonist-opioid and the patient does not have a mild-to-moderate-full-agonist-opioid-withdrawal and there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not conduct a standard-buprenorphine-initiation for the patient.
